{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Speak to Aaron, etc., saying.</b> It says a second time <b>saying</b>. Perhaps it is because the verse was concerned to say that it is merely optional — therefore Scripture says ״לֵאמֹר״, for it is a positive commandment to say it. Further, it intends that it was not to Aaron and his sons who were then present alone that He commands, but also to the generations. Further, it alludes to a language of exaltation, to say that this commandment carries the authority of the King to fulfill the matter; and there is also a distinction for the priests, for HaShem placed the blessings in their hands — and this is what it says: ״Speak, etc., saying.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:22.059659309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}